# The SPA's catch-all is gone.
#
# It read `/* /index.html 200`, which is what a client-side router needs: every
# path serves the homepage and Navigo decides what to show. Under Eleventy every
# page is a real file, and keeping the catch-all would turn every 404 — including
# a typo'd link to /privacy — into a silent homepage, which is worse than a 404.
#
# The old SPA route fragments, for anyone following a link that is now years old.
# /privacy is deliberately not a destination anyone is redirected to: it keeps its
# own URL and is simply not linked from the page (Nandan, 2026-08-25).

/overview   /         301
/studies    /         301
/software   /#code    301
/jobs       /         301
